cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, its data or its tools, please cite it as below."
title: "Polymarket, Home of the Insiders: on-chain investigations of Polymarket and the phi-forensics toolkit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Da Cunha"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/searadacunha/POLYMARKET-HOME-OF-THE-INSIDERS"
url: "https://github.com/searadacunha/POLYMARKET-HOME-OF-THE-INSIDERS"
abstract: >-
  A public archive of forensic investigations of Polymarket accounts and markets: funding and withdrawal
  tracing on Polygon and across chains, reconstruction of positions and trading results from chain logs,
  graded links between wallets, frozen-protocol studies with their negative results, and offline checks that
  re-verify each published figure from archived evidence. It includes phi-forensics, a read-only Python
  toolkit, command line and Model Context Protocol server built on the same methods. The frozen studies of
  the repository validated no detection rule as predictive.
keywords:
  - polymarket
  - prediction markets
  - blockchain forensics
  - on-chain analysis
  - wallet clustering
  - cross-chain tracing
  - reproducible research
  - model context protocol
